  "verdict": "REPLICATED",
  "coverage_pct": 100,
  "agreement_pct": 93,
  "justification": "Using the updated RefSeq NC_000964.3 (same B. subtilis 168 strain), essentially all genome-wide fractional metrics (GC, coding density, start codons, CDS base composition, and co-orientation) reproduce the paper’s values within ≤1 percentage point, and the rRNA operon count matches exactly (10). The genome size differs by ~796 bp (0.019%), which is expected given Barbe et al. (2009) error-correction re-sequencing and is effectively identical for reproducibility. The only notable discrepancy is tRNA loci (86 vs 88) and a modestly higher CDS count (4237 vs “~4,100”), both consistent with annotation drift and the paper’s explicitly approximate phrasing for CDS number."
}
